SSTTDDIINN
       If no files are given on the command-line and no files or expressions
       are given by the --ff, ----ffiillee, --ee, or ----eexxpprreessssiioonn options, then dc(1)
       reads from ssttddiinn.

       However, there is a caveat to this.

       First, ssttddiinn is evaluated a line at a time.  The only exception to this
       is if a string has been finished, but not ended.  This means that,
       except for escaped brackets, all brackets must be balanced before dc(1)
       parses and executes.

