       error (see the EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS section) if it cannot write to ssttddoouutt, so if
       ssttddoouutt is closed, as in ddcc  >>&&--, it will quit with an error.  This is
       done so that dc(1) can report problems when ssttddoouutt is redirected to a
